CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --apply-loop-contracts
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^\[check\.assertion\.\d+\] line \d+ assertion \*s->q == 0: FAILURE$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Checks that an address stored in a field of a local struct is reachable
through that struct: `check` reads the previous iteration's `t` through
`s.q`, so `t` is not a loop local.
